"""IDX 26 scenario fixture data — OPORD v2 (Operation BALTIC RESTORE).

Cougaar-fused KG entities, weather forecast, terrain layers, and project docs
for the V Corps MDAT-T/MDAT-SU exercise scenario.

Scenario clock — IDX 26 D-Day per OPORD v2 §3.b is "H-hour TBD"; the
existing `281200Z` DTG anchors the pre-attack INTSUMs / SITEMP / IPB
products. `current_dtg` carries the authoritative DDHHMMZmonYY anchor
that the runner uses to compute downstream header DTGs.

Threat: Donovian Corps (≈35 000 troops, three Mech/Mtzd Inf Divisions)
has invaded southern Estonia and transitioned to deliberate defense
along the Kopu - Rongu - Osula line; three divisions abreast facing
south. HQ WESTERN ARMY at Tartu rear C2; corps reinforcing fires (362+
364 FA BDE, 167 ADA, 600 ENG, 62 AVN, 644 RECON, 676 SIG) vic Tartu.

Friendly: V Corps (HQ Udrupe, Latvia) attacks north from southern
border to destroy the Donovian Corps and restore Estonian sovereignty.
1st ID main effort through Valga crossing → Kopu; 1st AD supporting
attack fixes 62 MTZD INF DIV at Rongu; 1st CAV screens east toward
66 MTZD INF DIV (Osula).

Authoritative sources:
  - OPORD v2 + Annex A/B/C — task org, locations, PIRs, scheme of maneuver
  - FIRST_DATA_DUMP/DONOVIA *.xlsx UNIT INFO sheets — full Donovian DIV/
    BDE/BN structure with verbatim names, SIDC codes, UIC, class templates.
  - Maa-amet INSPIRE GN + OSM Estonia/Latvia gazetteers — geocoding of all
    13 OPORD-named towns/villages (Kopu, Rongu, Osula, etc.) to authoritative
    coords; MGRS recomputed at 10-m precision via pymgrs.

Phase 1 (Penetration / Valga crossing) begins H-hour.
Phase 2 (Destruction Kopu-Rongu-Osula defensive line) begins +24h.
Phase 3 (Consolidation / restore border) projected H+72h.

Rename per OPORD v2 §1.a: 64 MTZD INF DIV  →  62 MTZD INF DIV
(XLSX was authored before OPORD v2 finalized the divisional designations).
Legacy "11th Mech Bde" scenario removed entirely (not in OPORD v2 OOB).
"""

SCENARIO_MONTH_YEAR = "JUN26"

# Per-product map RENDER fallback bbox — the CONOP bbox the IDX 26
# analysts picked for Operation BALTIC RESTORE. Order:
# [west, south, east, north] (lon/lat WGS84). Single source of truth
# for every per-product render; analyst pan/zoom in the operations-map
# editor persists per-product (tool_render_map GETs the per-product
# map UUID's stored bbox before falling back to this constant).
#
# DO NOT substitute either of:
#   - [25.5, 57.5, 28.0, 58.5]  — the old too-tight Voru-Tartu zoom
#     that's been the recurring regression. Every per-product render
#     with this value crops off the AAs' starting points and most of
#     the Latvian flank. The user has reverted this value repeatedly;
#     do not "restore" it under any "consolidation" rationale.
#   - [20.83, 55.77, 32.92, 60.22]  — the full Annex C polygon used
#     by the OFFLINE PRELOAD scripts only (covers Estonia + Latvia +
#     Lithuania + slices of Sweden / Finland / Russia / Belarus). Per
#     memory feedback_idx26_full_aor_bbox.md, preload-only — too zoomed
#     out for per-product renders.
#
# The CONOP value below is the one from commit a7e99fd's own message:
# "Operation BALTIC RESTORE, AO at CONOP bbox 24.238..28.614 /
# 57.092..58.634".
AO_BBOX = [24.238, 57.092, 28.614, 58.634]


